if you've seen any of the thor ragnarok  trailers then you'll know that as god  has a new villain who goes by the name  of hella but who is she and where did  she come from in Norse mythology hell is  the daughter of Loki making her the  sister of both Fenrir and young meg and  all of Loki's children were eventually  banished from Asgard  and hell was no exception shortly after  her birth she was banished by Odin to  hell more commonly known as the realm of  Helheim where the dead reside she made  Helheim her kingdom where she would rule  over the dead and the banished as the  goddess of the underworld hell's task  was to determine the fate of those who  entered the realm of the dead those who  died in battle would not be sent to hell  instead they went to Valhalla her  appearance is described as being half  black half white with a perpetual brim  and fierce expression on her face the  Vikings believed Hell to be half dead  and half alive and are often fearful of  her the German barbarians viewed hel as  having two sides light and dark being  helpful in times of need and vengeful to  those who cross her the most common  depiction of Hell is that of a greedy  and cruel leader indifferent to the  concerns of both the living and the dead  unfortunately Hellas character is not  mentioned much in Old Norse literature  and she's normally mentioned only in  passing one of the early surviving myths  to feature hell in detail is the death  of Balder the beloved Balder had been  slain by Loki and as a result was sent  to hell  upon arriving in Helheim the gods  emissary explained to hell that every  living thing was in mourning because of  the death of Baal dear she agreed to  release Balder  if every living thing in the universe  shed a tear for him there was one giant  who refused to shed a tear presumed to  be Loki in disguise because of that one  refusal her terms were not met and she  decided to keep Boulder in the  underworld from this story we can see  that Heather's character is similar to  that of her father's with not much known  about the character it'll be interesting  to see what direction mod will take with  her and what aspects of Norse mythology  they keep if you've enjoyed this video  then please go ahead and leave it a like  consider subscribing if folklore  mythology is something that interests  you if you have anything you'd like to  discuss or have any ideas for future  videos then please go ahead and let me  know in the comments below as always  I've been your host mythology and  folklore explained
 

